 "poem": "This Thursday, you left our\nTuesday at the door and never\nReturning till now by night before;\nThe great host there for morn or even\nThis time of year in summer weather\nFor table, and fruit basket,\nAnd Sunday school on the green lawn, etc.\nHad he his flowers no more before\nThan these which now lie in a jar? etc.\nHe lived as we think him, but here again\nWe read it harder than he when writing,\nSinging or playing, singing",
